| editorial =
'''The fourth man'''

Nishikawa Daigo brought a briefcase. Inside: 14 months of evidence. He waited for the chairman to be arrested before coming forward. He was afraid. That is human. That is also the system — a system where fear of retaliation keeps the truth in a briefcase until the handcuffs are on someone else.

The prosecution now has four defendants, one cooperating witness, and 22 minutes of audio. The IAA Commission has its first fully resourced case. The pension fund audit begins Monday. The workers are still waiting.

